%% PR watch (PR 11): a watch stores a target, not a session id. Delivery resolves it each time through
%% targets.ts, so a dead owner heals (a specialist refills, a thread revives) instead of freezing the watch.
%% The read position (lastCheckedAt, comment/review ids, CI status) moves only when the update lands.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant D as bridge-dispatch.ts / bridge-server.ts
    participant W as pr-watch.ts
    participant GH as GitHub API
    participant T as targets.ts
    participant SD as specialist-deliver.ts
    participant R as recovery.ts
    participant L as session-lifecycle.ts
    participant S as session (bridge)

    Note over D,W: A. Watch: the target is derived once, from the watcher
    D->>W: watchPr(url, watcher)
    W->>W: to = "main" | specialistForThread(thread) | thread id + revive
    W->>W: store prUrl, to, revive, threadId for the pin, read position

    Note over W,S: B. Poll (3 min): nothing is seen until it lands
    W->>GH: PR, comments, reviews, checks since the read position
    GH-->>W: new items, or none: persist and stop
    alt merged or closed
        W->>W: unwatch, unpin
    else new items
        W->>W: hold the current read position aside, build the update
        W->>T: deliverToTarget(to + revive, update), keyed by the next read position, queued, low priority
        alt to = specialist
            T->>SD: ensureSpecialist: dead → refill under the target lock
        else to = thread id, revive
            T->>R: reviveThreadForDelivery: resume → fork → fresh, back-off
        else to = main
            T->>S: main is never revived
        end
        T->>S: deliverToSession (queue while it boots)
        alt ok (delivered, queued, or duplicate key)
            T-->>W: ok
            W->>W: persist the new read position
        else 3, 4, 5, 6, 7: not landed
            T-->>W: exit + reason
            W->>W: restore the held read position: owed, fetched and sent again next poll
        else 8 or permanent
            T-->>W: no such specialist / too large
            W->>W: drop the watch, say why in its thread
        end
    end

    Note over W,L: C. Lifecycle: the target outlives its sessions
    L->>L: killSession with keepWatches (handoff, replacement, revive teardown) or keepRecord (reap): watches stay
    L->>W: any other kill (hydra kill, kill_session, done, a deleted thread): unwatchBySession (not for a guest)
    R->>W: recovery dedup: retargetWatches, a skipped sibling's watches to the winner's thread
